Final review complete — **no blocking findings**.

The review artifact is written and formatted at `.oat/projects/shared/recon-skill/reviews/final-code-review-2026-08-31T234514Z.md`, with `oat_review_invocation: gate` and the exact gate invocation metadata in its frontmatter, and all four severity headings set to `None`.

What the final pass covered and found:

- **Scope:** the full project diff against the `origin/main` merge base — 81 commits, 120 files (21 of them OAT bookkeeping) at head `8bad1e03`. All six phases/revisions had already closed with passing terminal reviews and there is no deferred-findings ledger.
- **Direct code verification:** I re-read the highest-risk surfaces independently — the packet validator and frozen `ValidatedRun` boundary, closed-object artifact contracts, symlink/containment path safety, canonical JSON hashing, the pack dependency-lease expansion (correct acquire-before-parent / parent-before-release ordering with deduplication), the user-materializable agent scanner (explicit source-mismatch and collision errors prevent pack agents shadowing built-ins), and the `tools.requiredBy` config normalization (rejects self-leases and unknown packs). Nothing rose to a finding at any severity.
- **Fresh test evidence, all green:** recon node suites; full `pnpm test:skills` (746/746); focused CLI vitest over all 23 changed-area test files (739/739); `oat:validate-skills`; `check:skill-bumps` (recon new at 1.0.0, `oat-dispatch-subagents` 1.2.3 → 1.2.4); and lockstep versions at 0.2.51 versus 0.2.50 on `origin/main`.

Verdict: pass. The project is releasable and the implement exit gate can close.Both background test runs were already accounted for in the review: the full skill suite passed 746/746 and the focused CLI suites passed 739/739. Their results are cited in the verification evidence of the final review artifact, so no follow-up is needed. The final review stands: no blocking findings, project releasable.
